append_md('SP61_CW_75_notes.md',r'''## Scan 020

The top paragraph recovers any transport-compatible vector space attached to a polygon from its value on the standard polygon and the dihedral action on that value. Item ⑤ is headed “Extension du groupe d’opérateurs,” replacing abbreviated “Changᵐᵗ de.” It introduces extension along a change of group, compares contracted products, and begins the torsor formulation continued on scan 021. No date or authorial page count; pencil archive number 19.

**Mathematics and reading.** The first group connector is a plain dash. The definition’s live exponent lies to the right: `E^{G′}`; the left exponent is cancelled. This is material because H combines a live left exponent with the right-handed product. The inserted direction after G-ens changes g to dr. Nonetheless, the definition still ends “comme G′-ens. à g.”, and the NB gives F a right action and then explicitly says “G ens à droite.” These words remain as written.

Under the earlier right-torsor/left-object convention, `E×_G G′` naturally has a right G′ action. The associativity formula is valid with E a right G-set, G′ its usual left-G/right-G′ biset, and F a left G′-set. This conditional check is S020-ASSOC; it does not turn the sheet’s conflicting direction words into a consistent convention. Two small products that H writes as wedges have visible crossing strokes and are transcribed as products. The lone i.e. after the long cancelled row is live: the strike stops before it.

The cancellation after the first paragraph’s récupérer leaves a low index under P. The older twist before the live left-twist has a T-like group low on the right of E, so E_T is preferred over E^T while both remain open. The short raised word replacing Alors is uncertain (soit/les), and its grammar is not used to settle it. There is no explicit authorial “à vérifier” on this sheet.''')
append_md('SP61_CW_75_doubts.md',r'''### Scan 020 — certainty-only decisions

The upper abbreviation is rg, not full rang; the group-change stroke is blunt. The overwritten g in the inserted direction and the old `G′×_G` after the defining equals sign are recoverable. “aussi,” “Pour,” and “donc on a” are readable. The small equals in `D_n=Aut(P_n)` has two short extended strokes (crop (494, 580, 861, 668)); it is retained. Several crossed exponents remain doubtful. The placement of mt in the cancelled heading and of the raised direction ending changes the representation and has a change row.''')
append_md('SP61_CW_75_hand_log.md',r'''## Added on scan 020

- **Tiny equals signs can have a curved upper stroke.** The sign in `D_n=Aut(P_n)` has two short extended strokes, unlike the two dots after G on scan 019. This is not a rule to read every pair of marks as an equality.
- **Raised abbreviation endings survive cancellations.** The old heading has Chang with raised mt; the NB direction probably has dr with raised te. H expands both. The second remains explicitly doubtful.
- **Overwriting preserves the earlier descender.** The g beneath the new d in the inserted “à dr” remains visible as a low loop. H reads the old direction as live.
- **Small product crosses may resemble wedges.** The two operators in the simplified contracted-product formula have a second crossing stroke. H writes wedge twice; the larger nearby products corroborate the local shape.
''')
checks([('S020-RECOVERY','used and rechecked in this run','For a transport-compatible assignment E(-), evaluating each isomorphism P_n→P sends E(P_n) to E(P). The evaluation descends through Isom(P_n,P)×^{D_n}E(P_n), and choosing one isomorphism makes it a linear isomorphism. This rechecks the scan 019 evaluation construction in the polygon case.'),('S020-ASSOC','targeted proof check','With E a right G-set, f:G→G′, and F a left G′-set, [[e,h],x]→[e,hx] gives (E×_G G′)×_{G′}F≅E×_G F. The G and G′ balancing relations give equal images; [e,x]→[[e,1],x] is the inverse. If E is a G-torsor, choosing e identifies E×_G G′ with the right regular G′-torsor. This checks the formula with coherent handedness, not the conflicting words à g./à droite in the source.'),('S020-SIDES','targeted proof check','Compared the direction words with the previously used right-first/left-second contracted product: the live wording does not match those inputs, while the formulas fit S020-ASSOC. No correction to direction words was made and no unconditional proof of the source wording is claimed.')])
